    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1082">

                <pb facs="1114" n="1100" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00/1411a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in El
                        Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-13T21:00:00-04:00">May 13, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. You are authorized to acknowledge receipt on May 16 in appropriate terms of
                    the note transcribed in your telegram no. 164 of May 12, thereby showing the
                    purpose of this Government to continue normal diplomatic relations with the
                    incoming Salvadoran administration. A circular telegram is being addressed to
                    the missions in <pb facs="1115" n="1101" xml:id="pg1101"/> the other American
                        Republics<anchor n="30" xml:id="d1082-f1"/> informing them of this and
                    instructing them to inform the governments to which they are accredited of this
                    Government’s intention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1082-f1" n="30" xml:id="d1082-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed on May 13 to diplomatic representatives in all the American Republics
                    except Bolivia, Argentina, and El Salvador; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
